<newsitem itemid="180937" id="root" date="1996-11-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Triplex Lloyd H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Triplex Lloyd H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.1		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.5		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    6.2		    vs 3.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   98.4		   vs 97.9</p>
<p> Operating profit	 6.92		   vs 5.92</p>
<p> Exceptional		0.1 profit	   vs 1.48 loss</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.77		   vs 1.1</p>
<p> Tax			  1.59		   vs 1.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  4.66		   vs 2.39</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 21, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 26  Ex-div date		November 18</p>
<p>NOTE - UK engineering group Triplex Lloyd Plc said it was &quot;encouraged by the bouyant level&quot; of its order books and remained confident for the future.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
